            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 28,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we fix this?  I don't know why it has \"Restart=no\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 28,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for pointing this out.\nThe `Restart=no` has been there since the multi-gpio-monitor service was first added in [26686] (2019). In 2020, [28554] updated the single-GPIO phosphor-gpio-monitor@.service from `Restart=no` to `Restart=always`, but the multi-GPIO service was not included.\nI've posted a fix in [88437] to align it.\n\n[26686]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-gpio-monitor/+/26686\n[28554]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-gpio-monitor/+/28554\n[88437]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-gpio-monitor/+/88437"
                }
            ],
